  "description": "Exact S3 orbit / stabilizer structure of the 52 vertex spun-normal surfaces of the Borromean rings complement B3 (SnapPy L6a4, 8 ideal tetrahedra, 3 cusps), for the idea-B3 pn-capability question: which surface classes decorate the three cusps asymmetrically and can carry a (Z,N)-distinguishing collective binding term. The census is re-derived via the same SnapPy machinery as the W9 angle-LP probe (m004 convention re-pin sigma=(1,2,0), eps=-1; GHHR 1604.02688 Prop A.3 pairing) and gated on EXACT per-index agreement with the committed W9 witness. The 48 isometries (full S3 on cusps; order-8 sign kernel K) act on the Z^6 peripheral grading via their cusp maps (convention pinned empirically by census-multiset preservation); the induced action on the 46 (slope, chi) classes gives K-orbits (unsigned peripheral classes), the S3 action on K-orbits (well-definedness machine-verified), S3 orbits, and exact stabilizers. Emits the cusp-support table, the refined orbit/stabilizer table, the asymmetric-class counts, the H-orbit DOF count for a labeling-stabilizer-equivariant weighting, and non-additivity data (tetrahedra-touched, pairwise-sum extremality). Structure-hunt tier; audit-only; scope-(a); NO FIT; no q0; no comparison to any binding observable; nothing wired to production.",
